---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base lang="en" title="Open JXL - Preview JPEG XL (.jxl) files in your browser" description="Local JPEG XL viewer. Check support, preview a .jxl file, save JPG or PNG. Nothing uploaded." path="/">
<section class="hero">
<span class="eyebrow">100% local | No upload | Free</span>
<h1>Open <span class="grad">JPEG XL</span> files right in your browser</h1>
<p class="lead">Got a <strong>.jxl</strong> file you cannot open? Drop it below to preview it on your device, then save as JPG or PNG when you need to share it.</p>
<p id="tagline2" hidden></p>
<div><span id="status" class="pill"><span class="dot"></span><span>Checking?</span></span></div>
</section>

<section class="tool-card" aria-label="JXL viewer">
<div class="tool-head"><span class="step-n">1</span> Drop your .jxl file <span style="color:var(--muted);font-weight:500">? one file, decoded on this device</span></div>
<div id="drop" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Choose a .jxl file">
<div class="drop-icon"><svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"/><polyline points="17 8 12 3 7 8"/><line x1="12" y1="3" x2="12" y2="15"/></svg></div>
<div id="drop-title">Drop a .jxl file</div>
<div id="drop-sub">or click to choose, paste also works</div>
<div class="drop-kbd"><span class="kbd">.jxl</span><span class="kbd">drag &amp; drop</span><span class="kbd">Ctrl/? + V</span></div>
<input id="file" type="file" accept=".jxl,image/jxl" hidden />
</div>
<p id="wasm-note"></p>
<div id="err" hidden></div>
<div id="loading" hidden><div class="spinner"></div><span id="loading-t">Decoding on this device?</span> <span id="secs">0</span>s</div>
<div id="result" hidden>
<div class="tool-head" style="border:none;padding:0 0 14px"><span class="step-n">2</span> Preview &amp; export</div>
<div class="result-grid">
<div class="preview-frame"><img id="preview-img" hidden alt="jxl preview" /><canvas id="preview" hidden></canvas></div>
<div>
<div class="chips"><span id="meta" style="display:contents"></span><span class="chip hot">Local only</span></div>
<div class="dl-row">
<button id="dl-jpg" class="btn primary" disabled>Download JPG</button>
<button id="dl-png" class="btn ghost" disabled>Download PNG</button>
</div>
<button id="again">Open another file -></button>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sections">
<div class="card"><div class="svg-ico"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#4f46e5" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"/></svg></div><h3>Private by design</h3><p>Files are decoded in your device memory only. Close the tab and they are gone - our servers never see your images.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="svg-ico"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#4f46e5" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polygon points="13 2 3 14 12 14 11 22 21 10 12 10 13 2"/></svg></div><h3>No install needed</h3><p>No software, no plugins. If your browser lacks native JPEG XL support, a local decoder kicks in automatically.</p></div>
<div class="card"><div class="svg-ico"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#4f46e5" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2"/><circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="1.5"/><polyline points="21 15 16 10 5 21"/></svg></div><h3>Share anywhere</h3><p>Export to JPG or PNG in one click, ready for albums, chats and social apps.</p></div>
</section>

<section class="card intro">
<h2>What is JPEG XL (.jxl)?</h2>
<p>JPEG XL is a modern image format designed to replace aging JPEG with smaller files and higher quality. If you received a <strong>.jxl</strong> file and wonder how to open a JXL file, you are in the right place: drop it into the viewer above to preview it instantly on your device, then save a JPG or PNG copy for apps that do not speak JPEG XL yet.</p>
</section>

<section class="faq">
<details open><summary>What is a .jxl file?</summary><p>A still image in the JPEG XL format -- efficient,, but not every app can open it. <a href="/how-to-open-jxl-file/">How to open -></a></p></details>
<details><summary>Is it safe to drop my file here?</summary><p>Yes. Decoding happens entirely in your browser. <a href="/privacy/">Privacy notes</a></p></details>
<details><summary>Is Open JXL free?</summary><p>Yes, free for viewing and exporting JPG/PNG. No account, no watermark.</p></details>
<details><summary>Why can't my browser open it?</summary><p>Native support varies by browser version. <a href="/jxl-browser-support/">Test this browser -></a></p></details>
</section>

<script is:inline src="/viewer.js" data-lang="en"></script>
</Base>
